    "title": "Goliad High School excels in district cross country meet - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Max Williams- ,\n6 hours ago Goliad cross country competes hard at district meet We look at how Goliad cross country did at the district meet\nGOLIAD, Texas- This week is district cross country time all across Texas. Goliad High School varsity girls and boys teams placed high at districts with boys team becoming district champions and girls team finishing in third place.\nFor the girls team, Cassidy Meyer finished in fifth place with a time of 12:51.931. Then Maely Brandes finished in eighth place with a time of 13:05.824.\nOther top scores for varsity girls team were Lily Knetl with a 14:15.771 and Taryn Franke getting her personal best with 14:38.312.\nAs for boys, they had three top 10 medal placers with Gabe Aguilar getting second place with a 17:40.567 and Jaiden Carranza got sixth place with 19:09.131 time.\nFor some of these runners, they will advance to regional meet in Corpus Christi on October 20th.",
